### COLD-READ SNIPPETS A to D (slides 39 to 42): instructor check only.
### Run section 1 of requests/s3-demos.sql first. Test book 0000000003 only.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### Snippet A: 204 ... then GET copy 2 below: 404, EVERY copy is gone. Re-run section 1 of the .sql.
DELETE http://localhost:3000/s3-snippet-a/books/0000000003/copies/1

### Snippet A check
GET http://localhost:3000/books/0000000003/copies/2

### Snippet B: 500, yet copy 3 WAS saved (check with the GET below)
POST http://localhost:3000/s3-snippet-b/books/0000000003/copies
Content-Type: application/json

{ "copyNo": 3, "rentalRate": 2.75 }

### Snippet B check: 200, the row is there
GET http://localhost:3000/books/0000000003/copies/3

### Snippet C: 200 with an empty body, even though copy 1 exists
GET http://localhost:3000/s3-snippet-c/books/0000000003/copies/1

### Snippet D: 500 ... then GET below: 200, the Book row survived the rollback (an orphan)
POST http://localhost:3000/s3-snippet-d/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isbn": "0000000005", "title": "Orphan Test", "yearPublish": "2026", "authorId": 999 }

### Snippet D check. Clean up with section 1 of the .sql.
GET http://localhost:3000/books/0000000005
